'''Teers''' was an [[Otolla]] [[Gungan]] [[Gender|female]] who served as a [[Rep]] on the [[Gungan High Council]] on her [[homeworld]] [[Naboo]]. She was in charge of the [[city]] [[Otoh Gunga]]'s power supply and, in [[32 BBY]], sat in the city's [[High Board Room]] while the [[Jedi]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] spoke before the council there. She agreed with [[Boss]] [[Rugor Nass]] when he scorned the [[Naboo (people)|Naboo]] people who the Jedi hoped to warn about a [[Trade Federation Droid Army|droid army]] [[Invasion of Naboo|invading]] Naboo. Teers was later nearby when Nass agreed to an alliance with the Naboo in the [[Gungan Sacred Place]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|A droid army is about to attack the Naboo. We must warn them.''"<br />"''Wesa no like da Naboo. Tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk. Da Naboo tink day so smarty. Day tink day brains so big.|Qui-Gon Jinn and Rugor Nass|audio=Jinn-Nass-NoLikeNaboo-TPM.wav|<ref name="TPM" />}}
Teers was an [[Otolla]] [[Gungan]] [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Geektionary" /> who was appointed by [[Boss]] [[Rugor Nass]]<ref name="FC">{{ForceCollection|Rep Teers|star=2}}</ref> as a [[Rep]] on the [[Gungan High Council]] that governed the Gungan people and ruled the [[city]] [[Otoh Gunga]]<ref name="CVD" /> on Teers' [[homeworld]] [[Naboo]].<ref name="GeektionaryFrench" /> Teers was in charge of the city's power supply<ref name="FC" />&mdash;which relied on [[plasma]] and [[bubble wort]] catalyst<ref name="SWCL">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref>&mdash;and acted as an important female voice on the council.<ref name="CVD" />

[[File:High_Tower_Boardroom.png|thumb|right|350px|Teers (fourth from the left) sat as a Rep on the Gungan High Council when they were visited by Qui-Gon Jinn and Obi-Wan Kenobi.]]
In [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the [[Jedi]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] were brought before the High Council<ref name="TPM" /> in the [[High Board Room]]<ref name="SWCL" /> of Otoh Gunga after the [[Exile (punishment)|exiled]] Gungan [[Jar Jar Binks]] led them to the city. Teers sat directly to the left of Nass in a floating seat with a [[plasma detonator]] beneath it while the Jedi explained that they wished to warn the [[Naboo (people)|Naboo]] people about a [[Trade Federation Droid Army|droid army]] that the [[Trade Federation]] had sent to [[Invasion of Naboo|invade]] Naboo.<ref name="TPM" /> The council refused to help,<ref name="French">''[[The Phantom Menace - The Film Novel]]''</ref> and Teers agreed with Nass when he scorned the Jedi,<ref name="Geektionary" /> stating that the Gungans had no love for the Naboo and that the [[droid]]s were unaware of Otoh Gunga and so posed no threat to his people.<ref name="TPM" />

Jinn then [[Mind trick|persuaded]] Nass to provide them with a [[Tribubble bongo|bongo transport]] to reach the Naboo, with the Boss directing them to travel through Naboo's [[Naboo Abyss|core]] to reach the Naboo [[capital]] [[Theed]]. As the Jedi left, Binks warned them that the council was setting them up for failure, as Naboo's core was extremely dangerous. Jinn then informed Nass that Binks owed him a [[life debt]] and so the Boss dismissed Binks to go with the Jedi rather than issuing another punishment upon the exile for returning to the city.<ref name="TPM" />

[[File:Nass_on_Sacred_Place.png|thumb|left|300px|Teers was nearby when an alliance was formed between the Gungans and the Naboo.]]
The invading droid [[army]] soon [[Attack on Otoh Gunga|forced]]<ref name="TPM" /> Teers<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2024 Topps Star Wars Hyperspace|cardname=Rep Teers &ndash; Naboo}}</ref> and the other Gungans to abandon Otoh Gunga and flee to their [[Gungan Sacred Place|sacred place]]. There, the Gungans were approached by [[Monarch of Naboo|Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] of the Naboo and her allies, who proposed an alliance between the natives of Naboo to defeat the Trade Federation.<ref name="TPM" /> Teers was nearby<ref name="Topps" /> when Nass accepted the proposal, after which the combined efforts of the Gungans and the Naboo [[Battle of Naboo|defeated]] the Trade Federation.<ref name="TPM" />

==Personality and traits==
Teers had [[Color|orange]] and white skin and yellow [[eye]]s.<ref name="CVD" />

==Equipment==
Teers wore a gray rep [[Clothing|hood]] and ornate brown and tan rep robes of office with silver [[Otoh swirls]] down the center.<ref name="CVD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Teers first appeared in the [[prequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']],<ref name="TPM" /> which was released on [[May 19]], [[1999]].<ref name="YbY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> Like all the secondary Gungans in the film, her computer-generated model was designed using the model for Jar Jar Binks as a base.<ref name="DB">{{DB|character|repteers|Teers, Rep}}</ref>

In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Teers's name was first used in the [[Star Wars video games|mobile card game]] ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'',<ref name="FC" /> which initially launched in [[2013]]. Although the launch of ''Force Collection'' predates<ref name="Force Collection release">{{SW|url=news/announcing-star-wars-force-collection|text=Announcing Star Wars: Force Collection|nolive=1}}</ref> the ''Star Wars'' canon reset of [[2014]],<ref name="Legends">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Leland Chee]] confirmed that the game was kept updated to fit with canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|holocronkeeper|status/846807700482666496|[[Leland Chee]]|quote=I'm not gonna go through the trouble of changing them and I don't have any reason to believe currently that anyone would. [&hellip;] On the off-chance that we DID have a current need to change any of these, we would have for Force Collection.|archivedate=20210505080831}} &mdash; [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] has confirmed that [[in-universe]] information from ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'' conforms with ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]].</ref> The [[Teers/Legends|name]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first used in ''[[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary]]'', a reference book written by [[David West Reynolds (real person)|David West Reynolds]]<ref name="TPMVD">''[[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> and released on [[May 26]], 1999.<ref name="Amazon">{{CollectorCite|6|Books with Bite}}</ref>

